**Rules:**
- One component per file, file named for the component, name in the project's
  casing convention.
- Props declared with a named type — never an inline object literal in the
  signature.
- Co-locate the style file with the component.
- No escape-hatch types (`any` and equivalents) — use explicit types.
- Never inject unsanitized HTML (`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` and its equivalents)
  without an explicit sanitizer.
- <!-- FILL: your state-management access pattern — the store/context/hook the
     component should read from, and the subscription style that avoids
     over-rendering (e.g. selector functions rather than whole-store reads).
     Delete this bullet if components in this project take state only via props. -->

